---
title: "Development Guide"
description: "qql-go development environment setup — build, test, lint, binary output, and dev workflow."
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

## Prerequisites

- **Go 1.24+**
- **Qdrant** (local Docker or Cloud)
- **buf** (optional, for proto regeneration)

## Setup

{% terminal title="Clone and Setup" %}
git clone https://github.com/srimon12/qql-go.git
cd qql-go
go mod download
{% /terminal %}

## Build

{% terminal title="Build Binary" %}
go build -o qql-go ./cmd/qql-go
{% /terminal %}

Debug build with source info:

{% terminal title="Debug Build" %}
go build -ldflags "-X main.Version=dev" -o qql-go ./cmd/qql-go
{% /terminal %}

## Test

{% terminal title="Run Tests" %}
# All tests
go test ./...

# Specific package
go test ./internal/parser/...
go test ./internal/filters/...
go test ./pkg/qql/...

# Verbose
go test -v ./internal/parser/...

# With coverage
go test -cover ./...
go test -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...
go tool cover -html=coverage.out
{% /terminal %}

## Lint

{% terminal title="Lint" %}
gofmt -l .
go vet ./...
{% /terminal %}

## Protobuf Regeneration

{% terminal title="Regenerate Protobuf" %}
buf generate
{% /terminal %}

Requires `buf` and the Go protobuf plugins. Generated files go to `gen/`.

## Run

{% terminal title="Run qql-go" %}
# After build
./qql-go version

# Go run (no build step)
go run ./cmd/qql-go version
go run ./cmd/qql-go connect --url http://localhost:6334
go run ./cmd/qql-go exec "SHOW COLLECTIONS"
{% /terminal %}

## Dev Workflow

1. Edit code
2. `go build -o qql-go ./cmd/qql-go`
3. `./qql-go exec "<statement>"`
4. `go test ./...`

## Integration Tests

Some tests require a running Qdrant instance. Start one:

{% terminal title="Start Qdrant" %}
docker run -p 6334:6334 qdrant/qdrant
{% /terminal %}

The test suite expects Qdrant on `localhost:6334` unless overridden by `QDRANT_URL`.

## Release Validation

Before tagging a release:

{% terminal title="Release Validation" %}
go run docs/dev_tasks.go release-validate --version <version>
{% /terminal %}

This checks:
1. Version sync (VERSION file, `commands.go`, CHANGELOG)
2. Quality checks (`gofmt`, `go vet`, `go test`, `go build`)
3. Binary build
4. Binary version output

## VS Code Setup

Recommended extensions:
- **Go** (golang.go) — language server, test runner
- **Error Lens** — inline error display
- **proto3** — syntax highlighting for `proto/qql.proto`

`.vscode/settings.json`:

```json
{
  "go.formatTool": "gofmt",
  "go.lintTool": "golangci-lint",
  "go.testOnSave": false
}
```
